    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0375" n="209" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/241</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-18T19:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 18, 1917, 7 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to my telegram of January 11, 6 p.m. Representatives of
                    International Corporation found Chinese authorities unwilling to entertain
                    proposal but they hope that Chinese authorities will agree to the issue of part
                    of the bonds at Tokyo. The American corporation could do the negotiations alone,
                    retaining the entire management. Carey has informed Japanese Legation who say
                    they will report favorably to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
